late or chewing gum. Sugar-glazed vegetables, fruit, or nuts are considered candied."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-candy"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candy"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Ukrainian cuisine","cuisine/ukrainian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Honey","ingredient/honey"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Sweetener","ingredient/sweetener"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Savas Kitchen: Ukrainian recipes","ref":"site/savaskitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"savaskitchen.com","note":"Ukrainian-born home cook Nataliia Savas's section of family Ukrainian recipes.","url":"https://savaskitchen.com/category/ukrainian-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Ukrainian cuisine","links":[["Angel wings","dish/angel-wings"],["Aspic","dish/aspic"],["Baba (cake)","dish/baba-cake"],["Banosh","dish/banosh"],["Blini","dish/blini"],["Borscht","dish/borscht"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Cabbage soup","dish/cabbage-soup"],["Cold beet soup","dish/cold-beet-soup"],["Custard","dish/custard"],["Gombovtsi","dish/gombovtsi"],["Gugelhupf","dish/gugelhupf"],["Halušky","dish/halusky"],["Kasha","dish/kasha"],["Kibinai","dish/kibinai"],["Kolach (bread)","dish/kolach-bread"],["Krupnik (soup)","dish/krupnik-soup"],["Kvass","dish/kvass"],["Medovukha","dish/medovukha"],["Mimosa salad","dish/mimosa-salad"],["Miodownik","dish/miodownik"],["Mors (drink)","dish/mors-drink"],["Palianytsia","dish/palianytsia"],["Pampushka","dish/pampushka"],["Paska (bread)","dish/paska-bread"],["Pie","dish/pie"],["Plăcintă","dish/placinta"],["Potato pancake","dish/potato-pancake"],["Rakott krumpli","dish/rakott-krumpli"],["Sauerkraut","dish/sauerkraut"],["Smetana (dairy product)","dish/smetana-dairy-product"],["Solyanka","dish/solyanka"],["Sorrel soup","dish/sorrel-soup"],["Soured milk","dish/soured-milk"],["Steak tartare","dish/steak-tartare"],["Syrniki","dish/syrniki"],["Tsvikli","dish/tsvikli"],["Uszka","dish/uszka"],["Varenyky","dish/varenyky"],["Vatrushka","dish/vatrushka"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/1/10/Candy_in_Damascus.jpg/500px-Candy_in_Damascus.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Elisa Azzali","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Candy_in_Damascus.jpg"}},"dish/dali-ni-horbo":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/dali-ni-horbo","n":"Dali ni horbo","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Batak cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Dali ni horbo, bagot ni horbo (water buffalo milk) is a  Batak dish from Tapanuli, North Sumatra, Indonesia."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-dali-ni-horbo"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dali_ni_horbo"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Batak cuisine","cuisine/batak-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Bromelain","ingredient/bromelain"],["Papain","ingredient/papain"],["Pineapple","ingredient/pineapple"]]},{"h":"More from Batak cuisine","links":[["Itak gurgur","dish/itak-gurgur"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/4/47/DALI_NI_HORBO%2C_KEJU_KHAS_SUKU_BATAK_1-5_screenshot.png/500px-DALI_NI_HORBO%2C_KEJU_KHAS_SUKU_BATAK_1-5_screenshot.png","w":500,"h":281,"by":"Televisi https://www.youtube.com/c/EfarinaTelevisi%7CEfarina Televisi","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DALI_NI_HORBO%2C_KEJU_KHAS_SUKU_BATAK_1-5_screenshot.png"}},"dish/dhokla":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/dhokla","n":"Dhokla","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Gujarati cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Dhokla or dokla is a savoury sponge dish that originated in the Indian state of Gujarat. It is made with a fermented batter that is steamed to a cake-like consistency. The batter consists of a mixture of rice with Bengal gram,, a variety of chickpea, but has several variants with the gram replaced by pigeon peas, or urad beans. In 2018, it was reported that Ahmedabad reportedly had daily consumption of 10,000 kgs of Dhokla."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-dhokla"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dhokla"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Gujarati cuisine","cuisine/gujarati-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Lentil","ingredient/lentil"],["Mustard oil","ingredient/mustard-oil"],["Sodium bicarbonate","ingredient/sodium-bicarbonate"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Spice Up The Curry (Andhra)","ref":"site/spiceupthecurry-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"spiceupthecurry.com","note":"Gujarati section of Kanan Patel's Indian vegetarian recipe blog.","url":"https://www.spiceupthecurry.com/category/recipes-by-region/gujarat/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Gujarati cuisine","links":[["Thepla","dish/thepla"],["Undhiyu","dish/undhiyu"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/d/d8/Dhokla_prepared_at_home%2C_Gurgaon%2C_India.jpg/500px-Dhokla_prepared_at_home%2C_Gurgaon%2C_India.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Tarunpant","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dhokla_prepared_at_home%2C_Gurgaon%2C_India.jpg"}},"ingredient/yomogi":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/yomogi","n":"Yomogi","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Artemisia princeps, also commonly called yomogi, ssuk, Japanese mugwort, Korean wormwood, Korean mugwort or wormwood in English, is an Asian plant species in the sunflower family, native to China, Japan and Korea. It is a perennial, very vigorous plant that grows to 1.2 meters (3 ft 11 in). This species spreads rapidly by means of underground stolons and can become invasive. It bears small, buff-coloured flowers from July to November which are hermaphroditic, and pollinated by wind. The leaves are feather shaped, scalloped and light green, with white dense fuzz on the underside."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-yomogi"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yomogi"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine",[["Kusa mochi","dish/kusa-mochi"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Mochi","ingredient/mochi"],["Red bean paste","ingredient/red-bean-paste"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/a/a1/Artemisia_princeps1.jpg","w":500,"h":383,"by":"KENPEI","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artemisia_princeps1.jpg"}},"dish/sobrassada":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/sobrassada","n":"Sobrassada","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Spanish cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Sobrassada in Catalan, or sobrasada in Spanish, is a raw, cured sausage from the Balearic Islands (Spain) made with ground pork, paprika, salt and other spices. Sobrassada, along with botifarró, are traditional Balearic meat products prepared in the laborious but festive rites that still mark the autumn and winter pig slaughter known as a matança in Minorca, Majorca and Ibiza. The chemical principle that makes sobrassada is the dehydration of meat under certain weather conditions (high humidity and mild cold) which are typical of the late Balearic autumn."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-sobrassada"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sobrassada"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Spanish cuisine","cuisine/spanish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Pork","ingredient/pork"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Spain on a Fork","ref":"site/spainonafork-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"spainonafork.com","note":"Albert Bevia's video channel and site of traditional and everyday Spanish recipes.","url":"https://spainonafork.com/welcome2/","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"}]},{"h":"More from Spanish cuisine","links":[["Andrajos","dish/andrajos"],["Bolinhos de bacalhau","dish/bolinhos-de-bacalhau"],["Buñuelo","dish/bunuelo"],["Caldo galego","dish/caldo-galego"],["Chistorra","dish/chistorra"],["Churro","dish/churro"],["Cocido","dish/cocido"],["Cuajada","dish/cuajada"],["Embutido","dish/embutido"],["Gazpacho","dish/gazpacho"],["Hojuela","dish/hojuela"],["Jamón","dish/jamon"],["Migas","dish/migas"],["Mojo (sauce)","dish/mojo-sauce"],["Patatas a lo pobre","dish/patatas-a-lo-pobre"],["Patatas bravas","dish/patatas-bravas"],["Picatostes","dish/picatostes"],["Pincho","dish/pincho"],["Pottage","dish/pottage"],["Salchichón","dish/salchichon"],["Salmorejo","dish/salmorejo"],["Soldaditos de Pavía","dish/soldaditos-de-pavia"],["Sopa de gato","dish/sopa-de-gato"],["Spanish omelette","dish/spanish-omelette"],["Spanish restaurant","dish/spanish-restaurant"],["Stuffed peppers","dish/stuffed-peppers"],["Tapas","dish/tapas"],["Turrón","dish/turron"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/f/f7/Sobrassada.jpg/500px-Sobrassada.jpg","w":500,"h":404,"by":"Slastic","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sobrassada.jpg"}},"cookbook/chez-panisse-cafe-cookbook":{"t":"book","r":"cookbook/chez-panisse-cafe-cookbook","n":"Chez Panisse Café Cookbook","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Cookbooks","cookbooks"]],"sub":"Cookbook by Alice Waters, 1999","square":true,"suggested":true,"isbn":"9780060175832","intro":[["Simpler ingredient-led dishes from the Chez Panisse upstairs café."]],"actions":[{"kind":"out","url":"https://openlibrary.org/isbn/9780060175832","label":"Open Library"}],"sections":[{"h":"Cuisines it covers","count":1,"links":[["California cuisine","cuisine/california-cuisine"]]}]},"cookbook/corsica-the-recipes":{"t":"book","r":"cookbook/corsi